<title>EGYPT: Egypt says buys extra 50,000 tonnes French wheat.</title>
<headline>Egypt says buys extra 50,000 tonnes French wheat.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt said on Sunday it was buying an extra 50,000 tonnes of French soft red wheat, making a total for the day of 450,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>The extra lot of 50,000 tonnes is from Sigma at $163.90 a tonne FOB, for loading any time in November, said Samir Shakankiri, vice chairman of the state's General Authority for Supply Commodities.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Wright +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
